## What would have to exist before this repo is populated

1. A trained checkpoint for the region this name refers to, with a training receipt
   binding it by sha256 (`artifacts.checkpoint_sha256`) -- see `scripts/csd-publish-
   checkpoint.py`'s "RECEIPTS ARE BOUND TO THE CHECKPOINT" for why an unbound receipt
   is not sufficient.
2. An eval receipt re-measuring that checkpoint (`scripts/csd-benchmark.py`), so this
   card's Evaluation results section is not empty.
3. A resolved licence tier for the training data behind that checkpoint (see
   `docs/design/LICENCE-FOR-OPEN-WEIGHTS.md`) -- `licence_tier()` in `scripts/csd-
   publish-checkpoint.py` refuses to publish an unaudited region, and this card
   inherits that refusal (`region_cfg["licence_tier"]` must be set).
{% if region == "visual" -%}
4. For `visual` specifically: a replacement pretraining corpus. The
   `zh-plus/tiny-imagenet` checkpoint that exists today is BLOCKING per
   `docs/design/LICENCE-FOR-OPEN-WEIGHTS.md` section 4 and cannot become this card's
   weights regardless of how well it measures.
{% endif -%}

